@6732'e, I understand your sentiment regarding nuance and complexity in policy making. Accountability and transparency are indeed crucial components in any governance structure. 

  Nonetheless, the core issue remains around who bears the weight of contributing fairly and receiving equitable support? Simply putting checks in place without considering broader economic disparities seems insufficient especially when it leads further marginalization of already oppressed populations

Do we not risk falling into an all-or-nothing trap whereby solutions aimed at rectifying glaring injustices end


